Status: DONE
GitHub issue: https://github.com/Zanark/BowserBoy/issues/106
Milestone: Reference-inspired cute screams and hard-landing face recovery.
Dependencies: Existing Pear BOY model, face tracking and drop lifecycle.
Purpose: Alternate the supplied scream expressions while lifted or falling,
then show angry, worried and normal faces after a hard landing without
losing the signature three dots on either cheek.

Tasks:
- [x] Add squeezed eyes, pink cheeks and alternating closed/open scream mouths.
- [x] Report downward support impacts without changing the existing trajectory.
- [x] Present angry, worried and normal recovery states in order.
- [x] Preserve all six permanent freckles, cancellation and reduced motion.
- [x] Review rendered close-ups and qualify actual drops and face clearance.

Acceptance criteria:
Lifted/falling Pear alternates scream mouths; hard support contact produces
angry, worried, then normal recovery. Minor drops and horizontal collisions
do not trigger anger. Every expression retains three visible dots per cheek.
Reduced motion holds the scream mouth still and permits static recovery.
Local technical verification is not user visual approval or deployment.

Completion evidence:
Syntax/build and all61unit tests pass, including two new support-impact
tests. Existing browser pickup and actual-painted-drop scenarios pass.
The drop records scared -> angry -> sad -> curious, with angry rebound.
Existing pickup coverage also verifies reduced-motion mouth stability and
frontmost freckle geometry in all four expressions at three gaze positions.
Reviewed actual rendered close-ups of normal, both scream mouths, angry
and worried faces. All six freckle centers are unobstructed in each.

Completion log:
2026-11-07: Add curved-shell facial geometry and paint-aware expression timing.
Close-up review finds angry eyes cover freckles; raise the eyes and move
blush marks below the dots. Correct worried brows to rise toward the center.
Expanded gaze-clearance regression finds a sad eye covering one freckle at
extreme gaze; raise sad eyes/glints. The repaired case passes with all
six dots frontmost at every tested expression/gaze. No new skip or timeout.
Changes remain local, uncommitted and undeployed; owner acceptance unrecorded.
